  "next_experiment": "Use offline emulator-state branching to obtain matched action-contrastive survival labels, then distill them into the unchanged online actor. Add a compact normal-enemy representation only as a separately ablated information intervention.",
  "conclusion": "Offline/online separation is operationally successful: a training-only risk head changes only the small actor and the final online path remains 1.474 ms p99. The future-safety student improves pre-boss held-out no-miss clears from 0/8 to 2/8 and full-stage held-out completion from 4/8 to 7/8. It does not solve perfect play: both full-stage conditions have 0/8 no-miss clears and student misses rise from 12 to 13. The method is retained for curriculum completion and rejected as sufficient survival credit."
